WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.570
So let's talk about just the crazy story out
of Mississippi, a Mississippi election commissioner

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.010
was caught on Facebook, I guess caught.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.940
I mean, I don't know if that's even the right
word.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:16.890
A posting on Facebook that the blacks are
registering to vote and that Mississippians

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:22.460
need to do something about it, sort of implying
that the blacks in Mississippi aren't really

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.720
the Mississippians.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.960
Obviously, this woman who did this is white.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.949
Now, for context, Mississippi is a state in
trouble.

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:37.120
If you look at American states ranked by Human
Development Index, which is a sort of composite

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.430
statistic of life expectancy, education and
per capita income.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.740
Mississippi is dead last.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.570
If you look at health care rankings, Mississippi
is dead last or sometimes forty eighth or

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:50.570
forty ninth.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.039
If you look at education rankings, Mississippi
is 46.

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:57.489
So Mississippi is a place with some serious
problems.

00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:02.780
Black folks make up a large percentage of
the Mississippi population.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.059
And good for them.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:05.489
They're registering to vote.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.570
They're holding voter registration drives.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.450
They plan to vote so that they can help their
state improve.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.560
In other words, you don't vote to ruin your
state.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.560
You vote to improve your state by having a
say in what it is that who is going to lead

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.780
you in what it is that they're going to do.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:28.950
Jones County Election Commissioner Gail Harrison
Welch posted on Facebook that she's concerned

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:33.210
that lots of the blacks are registering to
vote.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.630
That's it.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:35.630
That's her concern.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.630
There's no caveat.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.159
She says, quote, I'm election.

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:41.649
So I'm reading it as she wrote it.

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:42.649
I'm.

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:44.460
Election commissioner in Jones County.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.670
I'm concerned about voter registration in
Mississippi.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.540
The blacks are having lots of events for voter
registration.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:57.990
People in Mississippi have to get involved,
too, to thank you for all you do.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.180
By the way, before we get on this, this is
super funny.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:05.460
A guy named John Welch who shares her last
name and appears to be a family member, responded

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.330
to her Facebook comment by saying, quote,
Gail, you are no longer welcome at family

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.360
Reub reunion's.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.860
About 60 years ago, all parts of the Welch
family faced a choice.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.500
Racism or Americanism.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.120
The Virginia side of the Welch family from
the Shenandoah chose America.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.040
You are plainly wrong, which is absolutely
hilarious to see her family's dirty laundry

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.200
aired on Facebook.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.800
But eventually, because this was a public
post on Facebook, she was confronted about

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.760
her statement by the local newspaper, The
Clarion Ledger, and she said, quote, I don't

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.010
mean anything by it.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.270
I've worked hard to make sure everybody is
registered to vote black or white, everybody.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.990
That's just how I am now.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:50.880
In my experience, most people who refer to
the blacks doing something do mean something

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.160
by it that is racially tinged, if not straight
up racist.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:00.751
And also when she says the blacks are having
lots of events to register voters, people

00:03:00.751 --> 00:03:03.640
in Mississippi have to get involved, too.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:10.160
It is obviously implying that she sees black
Mississippians as not really the people of

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.160
Mississippi.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.850
It's the white people in Mississippi that
are really the people of Mississippi.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:21.320
Now, her other excuse, and this is crazy because
it's not an excuse her other excuse was the

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.200
message was meant to be sent as a private
message on Facebook.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.680
It wasn't meant to be public.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.140
I hate to break it to you.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.940
All that means is you had the sense to realize
it shouldn't be public.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.080
It should be private in order to avoid more
scrutiny.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.510
But it doesn't make it any less racist or
any more outrageous.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:45.520
And the real tragedy, and this is the sort
of circling around the real tragedy, is she

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.750
still has this position in Jones County in
Mississippi.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:57.380
She said this in a state that is more than
30 percent black and she is still an election

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.150
official in Jones County, Mississippi, at
least as of this morning.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.940
And if that changes, I will certainly let
you know.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:12.280
But this is you know, the right has this idea
that calling someone racist is the worst thing

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:13.490
you can do.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:19.440
And they've actually weaponized claims of
racism against those who make the claims.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:24.660
You see this very frequently where they've
also they've all almost made it taboo.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.100
They've tried to make it taboo to claim to
see racism.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:35.670
And they very often say that seeing racism
is the racism or seeing racism as, quote,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.490
playing the race card.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.940
That's like the phrase Trump derangement syndrome.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.410
These are phrases meant to just shut down
debate.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:46.590
They say on the right that the left wants
to shut down debate.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:52.380
When you tell anybody who has identified an
act of racism that the problem is then mentioning

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.700
it, that is a form of shutting down debate.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:05:00.800
Similarly, there's this phrase you're suffering
from TADS Trump derangement syndrome.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.280
When somebody on the Internet will make a
criticism of Donald Trump.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.360
Trump supporters will pop up and they'll say,
you're suffering from Trump derangement syndrome.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.990
This is a way to just shut down the debate.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:18.930
You're disqualifying the person making the
criticism as just being blinded by hatred

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.980
of Trump and being unable to speak coherently.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.910
What you're actually doing is you're shutting
down the person and not even having to defend

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:27.910
against the claims.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:32.280
That's the same type of thing that we see
with, oh, you've identified racism.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.700
You're the person who is actually racist.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.840
She is still an election official in Mississippi.

